            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 23 manifest paths for security, data loss and unsafe input handling. I found no reachable, candidate-caused risk.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: PlanUninstall refuses an id that is procedural or has no install record before anything is planned. It then reuses install's planSkill with an empty source. An edited, non-regular or unreadable recorded file refuses the whole uninstall, so nothing is removed. The id from the command line only selects a record and is never used as a path.",
              "engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go: removeEmptyTree only calls Remove on directories that hold nothing but empty directories. It never deletes a file and does not follow symlinks, so files the record does not list are kept and their directory is reported as kept.",
              "engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go: uninstall takes the exclusive project lock on the absolute working directory before reading or writing. A relative working directory is refused before locking. Dry run writes nothing, and the CLI test compares the whole tree before and after.",
              "Whether the paths in an install record are validated as staying inside the project is decided in the base planner, which this patch does not show or change. I report nothing about it.",
              "The project-status change only adds read-only output lines. The other files are docs, goldens, tests and receipts with no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
