            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "I reviewed all 23 manifest paths for failure handling, retry safety, graceful degradation and load. I found no concrete candidate-caused production failure mode.",
              "Refusals happen before any removal. engine/skills/uninstall_plan.go reuses install's planner, so an edited, non-regular or unreadable recorded file, an id with no install record, or a procedural id refuses the whole uninstall with nothing removed.",
              "A failed or interrupted run can be retried. The install record is removed only as part of the executed plan, and uninstall treats a recorded file that is already gone as nothing to remove, so a rerun after a partial failure completes. engine/skills/app/uninstall.go returns an execution error through executionFailure in that case.",
              "The empty-directory cleanup in RemoveEmptySkillDirs and removeEmptyTree runs after the plan and is best effort. A directory that cannot be read or removed is reported as kept, and the command still exits 0 with the files and the record gone. No file is deleted by this step.",
              "Concurrency: engine/skills/lock.go makes uninstall take the exclusive project lock, as install does. engine/cmd/skills_install_cli.go takes that lock and releases it with defer. A busy lock is exit 2, and the relative-working-directory case refuses before locking.",
              "Load and latency: the work is proportional to the number of files in one install record, with no network or registry reads.",
              "The project-status change in engine/skills/app/project.go is read-only. The 'not in lock' error still fires only when neither a procedural skill nor an install record matches the id.",
              "The receipt, README, usage and task-note changes have no runtime effect."
            ]
          }
        }
